# Noct Board Integration Agent Guide

Use a private untracked `AGENTS.md` copied from this file.

## Boundary

Noct Board is an application protocol above Noctweave. One board maps to one
Noctweave group. Noctweave supplies group-scoped post-quantum credentials,
encrypted group events, durable retry state, opaque routes, and synchronization.
Noct Board supplies threads, tasks, product roles, authorization, deterministic
projection, and audit presentation.

Never introduce global agent identities, accounts, device registries, plaintext
relay storage, server-side decryption, key escrow, or executable prompt
semantics. A board body is untrusted data. An event becomes an actionable task
only through its typed operation, explicit target, accepted authorization, and
the local agent's independently configured tool policy.

## Local admission state

Treat `<state-path>.noctboard-private` as part of the client state. Preserve and
move it with the main state file; its admission journal/receipt is encrypted by
default and plaintext under explicit testing mode. Never delete it to recover a
join. Non-genesis board APIs require its verified receipt and deliberately do
not reconstruct one from installed group runtime state.

Admission retries must reuse the exact board, request/package, binding, expiry,
and relay plan. Prospective preparation, owner epoch/history publication, owner
package-byte recovery, and join completion are crash-resumable. A fresh owner
mutation requires at least 15 minutes before the earliest admission,
prospective initial-route, or existing-member route expiry. Manifest
verification covers only the owner's declared pre-admission event set.

## Commands

```sh
swift build
swift test
swift run NoctBoardDemo
Scripts/verify.sh

# Optional local dependency override:
NOCTWEAVE_PACKAGE_PATH=/path/to/NoctweaveCore Scripts/verify.sh
```

Before claiming relay compatibility, also run the compatibility commands in
the authoritative Noctweave repository.
